Subject: [FIX] preserve the GXLX2 VPU DMC request on HEVC stop/start

The existing VLD exception did not cover HEVC. Its numerical >=G12 gate
adds bit8 on GXLX2, although the legacy map assigns bit8 to VPU read0.
Fault evidence: HEVC EOF, DMC_REQ_CTRL=deef (bit8 off), pending RDMA
read requests and empty read FIFO, with both completion channels stalled.
Exclude GXLX2 from HEVCB in both directions; preserve all other CPUs.
On the same 293H boot, restoring only bit8 (deef -> dfef) resumed both
completion channels and the shared IRQ, stopped the watchdog reset loop,
and restored the menu as confirmed by the user. Full ARM/module build
and source-built HEVC EOF/Stop/replay regression remain pending.

--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/utils/vdec.c
@@ -698,7 +698,9 @@
 		mask = vdec_vld_dmc_mask();
 	} else if (input->target == VDEC_INPUT_TARGET_HEVC) {
 		mask = (1 << 4); /*hevc*/
-		if (get_cpu_major_id() >= AM_MESON_CPU_MAJOR_ID_G12A)
+		/* GXLX2 bit8 is the legacy VPU read port, not HEVCB. */
+		if (get_cpu_major_id() >= AM_MESON_CPU_MAJOR_ID_G12A &&
+		    get_cpu_major_id() != AM_MESON_CPU_MAJOR_ID_GXLX2)
 			mask |= (1 << 8); /*hevcb */
 	}
 
@@ -738,7 +740,9 @@
 		mask = vdec_vld_dmc_mask();
 	} else if (input->target == VDEC_INPUT_TARGET_HEVC) {
 		mask = (1 << 4); /*hevc*/
-		if (get_cpu_major_id() >= AM_MESON_CPU_MAJOR_ID_G12A)
+		/* GXLX2 bit8 is the legacy VPU read port, not HEVCB. */
+		if (get_cpu_major_id() >= AM_MESON_CPU_MAJOR_ID_G12A &&
+		    get_cpu_major_id() != AM_MESON_CPU_MAJOR_ID_GXLX2)
 			mask |= (1 << 8); /*hevcb */
 	}
 
